==Battleground==
*6 [[Gardeneel Bros.]] spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Mega Baa Baa]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Wicked Face]] spawns as the boss after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*2 [[Fallen Bear]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Mega Baa Baa]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 66% HP:
**1 [[Mega Baa Baa]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 33% HP:
**1 [[Mega Baa Baa]] spawns.

==Strategy==
One of the best ways to clear this stage is to use huge sources of damage to kill Fallen Bear as quickly as possible. [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] is the most stellar example, dealing half of Fallen Bear's HP at Level 46 and skipping a knockback in addition to being able to push back Wicked Face, but can be difficult to time. Another option is using [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercers]] to bring down Fallen Bear's [[Shield]] before delivering a huge hit with the likes of [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]; [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] in particular can avoid Gardeneel Bros' Warps thanks to his high knockback count.

The lack of money in this stage may prove problematic without a Rich Cat, but good fortune with Gardeneel Bros' Warps can let you kill them every now and then and net an extra bit of cash.

==Trivia==
*Its name is a reference to the [[wikipedia:Great Barrier Reef|Great Barrier Reef]], a coral reef system located on the coast of Queensland, Australia.

